;; std's build for rsi (doc/rust/EVAL.md §3; RES3 (a)): the sysroot every lowered program and the judge are compiled against from
;; RE3 on, built by Cargo's -Zbuild-std from the pinned rust-src (tools/rsdump/apks.sha256) with the profile below, its LLVM IR kept
;; (-C save-temps: each codegen unit's bitcode, made IR text by clang -S -emit-llvm, survey P5) and pinned by digest
;; (test/rust/runtime/ir.sha256, bin/rsi std-build --update), as CX7 pins libstdc++'s (test/cpp/runtime/ir.sha256). bin/rsi
;; std-build checks the oracle and the assembler against :rustc and :clang first. Read with the Clojure reader.
{:rustc "rustc 1.99.1 (58cf8f9c3 2026-10-13) (Alpine Linux Rust 1.99.1-r0)"
 :clang "Alpine clang version 23.1.4"
 :target "x86_64-alpine-linux-musl"
 ;; Cargo's release profile, overridden (CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_*): -O0, no debug assertions and no overflow checks in std (as the
 ;; host's release std: its panics' texts are the judge's), unwinding panics, Cargo's default codegen units
 :profile {"OPT_LEVEL" "0" "DEBUG_ASSERTIONS" "false" "OVERFLOW_CHECKS" "false" "PANIC" "unwind" "DEBUG" "0" "TRIM_PATHS" "all"}
 ;; the target crates' flags (RUSTFLAGS; the build scripts' are Cargo's own)
 :rustflags ["-Csave-temps" "-Cembed-bitcode=yes"]
 :build-std "std,panic_unwind,panic_abort,proc_macro,test"}
